            <ArticleTitle>Computed tomography of the spine: curved coronal reformations from serial images.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>185-90</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A new imaging format described here uses nonplanar reformations that follow the contour of curved structures intersected by a series of regularly spaced CT scans. The CT scanning procedure is described, and algorithmic details of this new format are presented. A standard set of reformatted images is suggested, and clinical examples are given to illustrate the diagnostic value of this new format.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
